    "title": "Claremore Man Dead After Boating Incident on Oologah Lake - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matt Jordan ,\n1 days ago A Claremore man is dead following a boating incident on Oologah Lake. According to the Oklahoma Highway Patrol, the incident happened at around 11:00am yesterday morning in Will Rogers Cove on Oologah Lake in Rogers County. Troopers say 71-year-old Robert Johnson and his boat were reported missing to the Rogers County Sheriff's Office. A search involving the Oklahoma Highway Patrol Marine Division, Northwest Fire Department and the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers was launched. Read full article\n2",
